                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> "2026-05-11" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "OSBPL2 (ORP2) enables cholesterol/PI(4,5)P2 endosomal exchange  (Human)" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/pav/providedBy> "https://holthuis-lab-uos.de" ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "Monomer ORP2 transfer Cholesterol, homotetrameric ORP2 -PI4,5P2 (Based on structural information, the cholesterol‐bound ORP2 is monomeric and the PI(4,5)P2‐bound one tetrameric (Wang et␣al, 2019), i.e., four cholesterol molecules would be transported from late to recycling organelles by ORP2 monomers that assemble to a tetramer to transport four PI(4,5)P2 molecules back)" ;
